{"name":"Dubonnet","hex":"#5b2c31","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dubonnet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A French bittersweet red aperitif."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dubonnet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dubonnet","blocks":[{"text":"Dubonnet is a sweet, aromatised wine-based quinquina, often consumed as an aperitif. It is a blend of fortified wine, herbs, and spices, with fermentation being stopped by the addition of alcohol. It is currently produced in France by Pernod Ricard, and in the United States by Heaven Hill Distilleries of Bardstown, Kentucky. The French-made version is 14.8% alcohol by volume and the U.S. version 19%. The beverage is famous in the United Kingdom for having been the favourite drink of Queen Elizabeth II and Queen Elizabeth the Queen Mother."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Dubonnet_wine_ad_1915.png/330px-Dubonnet_wine_ad_1915.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dubonnet","wikidata":"Q266349"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Echo_du_Mardi_Gras_-_Publicit%C3%A9_pour_Dubonnet.jpg/500px-Echo_du_Mardi_Gras_-_Publicit%C3%A9_pour_Dubonnet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Echo_du_Mardi_Gras_-_Publicit%C3%A9_pour_Dubonnet.jpg/1280px-Echo_du_Mardi_Gras_-_Publicit%C3%A9_pour_Dubonnet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Echo_du_Mardi_Gras_-_Publicit%C3%A9_pour_Dubonnet.jpg/500px-Echo_du_Mardi_Gras_-_Publicit%C3%A9_pour_Dubonnet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dubonnet advertisement, 1907 — Napoleon and Madame de Pompadour share a bottle during Fat Tuesday of carnival. The caption, idiomatically rendered, roughly says: (Napoleon Bonaparte to Mme. the Marchioness de Pompadour) \"My dear Marchioness, you seem frozen, come down from your carriage and have a glass of Dubonnet. If, at the time, I had but had a few thousand bottles, my retreat from Russia would have changed into a march of triumph!\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEcho_du_Mardi_Gras_-_Publicit%C3%A9_pour_Dubonnet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Plakat_Cheret_95.jpg/500px-Plakat_Cheret_95.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Plakat_Cheret_95.jpg/500px-Plakat_Cheret_95.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dubonnet poster (1895)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlakat_Cheret_95.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Lautrec_-_Publicit%C3%A9_Dubonnet.jpg/500px-Lautrec_-_Publicit%C3%A9_Dubonnet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Lautrec_-_Publicit%C3%A9_Dubonnet.jpg/1280px-Lautrec_-_Publicit%C3%A9_Dubonnet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Lautrec_-_Publicit%C3%A9_Dubonnet.jpg/500px-Lautrec_-_Publicit%C3%A9_Dubonnet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Faded Dubonnet advertisement on a wall, Lautrec, 2018","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALautrec_-_Publicit%C3%A9_Dubonnet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Queen%27s_Dubonnet.jpg/500px-Queen%27s_Dubonnet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Queen%27s_Dubonnet.jpg/1280px-Queen%27s_Dubonnet.